    <!-- The uninstall's questions -->
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Uninstall.KeepTitle">Nextcalibur - keep or remove?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Uninstall.KeepBody" xml:space="preserve">Nextcalibur has removed its own files, settings and scheduled tasks.&#10;&#10;Two things it did to Windows can stay or go:&#10;{0}&#10;&#10;The power repair fixes a Windows fault and works whether or not Nextcalibur is installed; the plans are yours to keep using.&#10;&#10;Remove them as well?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Uninstall.DependencyTitle">Nextcalibur - {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Uninstall.DependencyBody" xml:space="preserve">Nextcalibur installed {0} for its own use: it {1}.&#10;&#10;Other programs may use it too. Remove it as well? If unsure, keep it; it does nothing on its own.</sys:String>

    <!-- The first run's power repair -->
    <sys:String x:Key="S.FirstRun.Repaired">Nextcalibur found and repaired a Windows power configuration fault:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.FirstRun.Found">Nextcalibur found a Windows power configuration fault.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.FirstRun.Undo">Your CPU can now idle down properly. You can undo this at any time from the Power Mode panel.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.FirstRun.RepairedTitle">Nextcalibur - power fault repaired</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.FirstRun.PartlyTitle">Nextcalibur - power fault partly repaired</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.FirstRun.Failed">Nextcalibur could not repair the Windows power overlay automatically:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.FirstRun.Retry">You can retry from the Power Mode panel.</sys:String>

    <!-- Settings page: the tools' dialogues -->
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Debloat.Title">Open Win11Debloat?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Debloat.Body" xml:space="preserve">This opens Raphire's Win11Debloat in an administrator PowerShell window: the script is downloaded from raphi.re and run. It is not part of Nextcalibur and nothing here vets it; what you choose there - ads, suggestions, apps, settings - is between you and it. Its author says its changes can be reverted (described in its wiki).&#10;&#10;Go on?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.WinUtil.Title">Open WinUtil?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.WinUtil.Body" xml:space="preserve">This opens Chris Titus Tech's WinUtil in an administrator PowerShell window: the script is downloaded from christitus.com and run. It is not part of Nextcalibur and nothing here checks it; what you change there - services, apps, settings - is between you and it.&#10;&#10;Continue?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.WinUtil.Failed">PowerShell could not be started:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Link.Failed">The browser could not be opened:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Privacy.Title">Privacy</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Privacy.Body" xml:space="preserve">Nextcalibur collects nothing about you and sends nothing about you anywhere.&#10;&#10;The only requests it makes are to GitHub, to find its own updates and PawnIO's - and none at all with automatic checks off - and they carry nothing of yours beyond what any download does. Settings and the log stay in your profile; nothing is uploaded unless you attach it to a report yourself. No account, no telemetry, no analytics.&#10;&#10;Open the full policy, with the list of every request, in your browser?</sys:String>

    <!-- Updates -->
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.Title">Nextcalibur - updates</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.ANewVersion">a new version</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.PortableCurrent">This copy was not installed by Setup, so it cannot update itself; the things it depends on are current.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.Checking">Checking for updates to Nextcalibur and what it depends on...</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.Latest">You have the latest version, and so do the things it depends on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.Unreachable">Could not reach GitHub to check:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.AvailableTitle">Nextcalibur {0} is available</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.AvailableToast">Download it and restart into it?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.AvailableBalloon">Click here to update.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.Now">Update now</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.PendingGraphics">A graphics mode change to {0} is waiting for a restart of Windows. Updating restarts Nextcalibur, not Windows, and the pending change is dropped: choose it again afterwards, or restart Windows first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.OfferTitle">Update to {0}?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.OfferBody" xml:space="preserve">Nextcalibur {0} is ready to install. Keeping it current matters more here than for most software: this application writes to your laptop's firmware, watches its temperatures and runs as administrator, and every release carries fixes to exactly those parts. An older version keeps the mistakes that have since been found - and, in a public project, published for anyone to read.&#10;&#10;You can put it off this once. The next time it comes up it is installed.&#10;&#10;Update now?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.Progress">Updating to {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.InstallingRestarting">Installing and restarting...</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.NoRestart">The update was downloaded but the application could not restart into it. Close and reopen Nextcalibur to finish.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.Failed">The update could not be installed:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.RequiredBody" xml:space="preserve">This update was put off once, and it is not put off twice. Nextcalibur writes to your laptop's firmware and runs as administrator; the fixes in each release are to those parts, and an older version keeps mistakes that are already known and published.&#10;&#10;It is downloaded now, and the application restarts into it. Your settings stay as they are.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.RequiredTitle">Nextcalibur {0} is being installed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Update.AtWindowsRestart">Nextcalibur {0} is downloaded. A graphics mode change to {1} is waiting for Windows to restart, and restarting Nextcalibur now would drop it - so the update goes in at that restart.</sys:String>

