    <sys:String x:Key="S.Cooling.Title">Heading for the warning line</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Cooling.Body">CPU {0} °C, GPU {1} °C and rising {2} °C a minute: {3}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Cooling.Cap">the processor is held to {0}%.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Cooling.Fans">press Fn+1 on the laptop's keyboard to put the fans at full speed before it gets there.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Cooling.Both">the processor is held to {0}% until it has cooled; Fn+1 on the laptop's keyboard puts the fans at full speed too.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Cooling.TurboStillOn">The fans are still at full speed. Fn+1 on the laptop's keyboard puts them back to normal.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Cooling.CooledTitle">Cooled down</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Runaway.Title">A program is heating the machine</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Runaway.Cpu">{0} has kept {1} processor cores busy for {2} minutes without a break, in the background. If it should not be working, close it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Runaway.Gpu">{0} has kept the graphics card busy for {1} minutes with nothing on screen needing it. If it should not be working, close it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Runaway.TaskManager">Open Task Manager</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.AutoCoolingTitle">Emergency Power Saver</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.AutoCoolingDesc">When the temperature heads for the warning line, the processor is held to Power Saver's speed until it cools.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.AutoFanTurboTitle">Warn before it gets hot</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.AutoFanTurboDesc">When the temperature heads for the warning line, you are told to press Fn+1 for full fan speed - only the laptop's own keyboard can.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Tour.Step.SettingAutoCooling.Title">Emergency Power Saver</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Tour.Step.SettingAutoCooling.Body">Off unless you want it. When the temperature is heading for the warning line, the processor is also held to Power Saver's ceiling - which turns the boost off - and let go after five minutes comfortably below the line. The machine is slower while it lasts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Tour.Step.SettingAutoFanTurbo.Title">Cool down before it gets hot</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Tour.Step.SettingAutoFanTurbo.Body">The temperature is followed, not just compared: when it is on its way to the warning line, a notification says to press Fn+1 before it gets there - the fan turbo, which the laptop switches only from its own keyboard - and, once it has been well below for five minutes, that the turbo can go off. Off: nothing is followed or said. On by default.</sys:String>
